## Director Directives Captured as Doctrines (memory entries)

Four NEW doctrines saved to `~/.claude/projects/C--SandyStudio/memory/` and indexed in MEMORY.md:

1. **`critic_revision_cap_doctrine.md`** — Critics MUST cap at N=2 (configurable) and emit HALT verdict on attempt N+1. Director sees in approvals queue, decides. Director's verdict = law, no further auto-REVISE loop. Currently only GAGAD has this (runner.ts:1163). EXEC-VPREV + EXEC-EPREV need it = TD-83.

2. **`plan_preview_drawer_doctrine.md`** — Plan asset opens as «pre-video contract page»: video placeholder reserving height (so post-Regenerate doesn't reflow) + prompt text area + settings grid + Approve/Reject/Regenerate footer. SAME shape as VID-shot drawer, just without rendered video. NOT raw markdown. Implementation = TD-84.

3. **`train_personnel_doctrine.md`** — Expanding agent data access without skill update = silent regression. Every TD touching loadAgentInputs/event payload MUST touch `agents/exec/*.md` skill file. Pattern: Director treats agents as employees, system prompt = training manual.

4. **`match_cut_doctrine.md`** — Empirical: `seedance-with-end-image` valid ONLY when next shot continues current at SAME angle. Different-angle cuts MUST use `seedance-standard` with `end_image: null`. Validated SH19 2026-05-27 by comparing two direct VGEN tests (SH20 end = wrong / SH22 end = right). Critic V09 should validate.

